(a) A person commits disorderly conduct if the person intentionally or knowingly does any of the following:

    (i) Engages in fighting or violent behavior;

    (ii) Makes unreasonable noise;

    (iii) Creates a hazardous or physically offensive condition by any act which the person should realize will alarm or seriously annoy others;

    (iv) Obstructs the free and unobstructed use of any public way;

    (v) Refuses to obey a lawful order issued by a law enforcement officer;

    (vi) Knowingly enters and remains upon the property of another after having been forbidden to do so;

    (vii) Knowingly goes upon the property of another with the intent to damage or destroy any property of the owner;

